      ":question/math-academy-id": "q-123917",
      ":question/problem": "Consider the finite region $D$ enclosed in the first quadrant of the $xy$-plane between the curves\n$y = x, y = 2x, y = \\frac{2}{x}, y = \\frac{6}{x}$.\nA transformation $T$, given by\n$T: (u, v) \u2192 (x(u, v), y(u, v))$,\nmaps a rectangular region $\u0394$ with sides parallel to the $u$- and $v$-axes from the $uv$-plane onto $D$ in the $xy$-plane. Given that\n$T^{-1}: (x, y) \u2192 (A A, xy)$,\nwhat could be the missing expression?"
